 "taxonomy_note": "Not in the ACO 2022 checklist (split from Grallaria quitensis); added from eBird/Clements 2025. Boyaca Antpitta, split from Tawny Antpitta (G. quitensis) by IOC (July 2023) and Clements (October 2023): Eastern Andes of Colombia (route: Chingaza, Sumapaz, the other Bogotá sites). G. quitensis stays for the Central Andes and Nariño (Bordoncillo, La Cocha). Not split by SACC/ACO and not in Chaparro-Herrera et al. 2024; `endemic` follows the Clements range (Eastern Andes of Colombia only).",
